<%# THE WORKFLOWS SURFACE for /deployments — the eight soul launchers (Turf
    Monster / Carl / Avi / Steffon / Mason / Alex / Mack / Pokémon), each a copyable heartbeat prompt
    (none for Pokémon, which has no HEARTBEAT) plus its
    acts. Titled "Workflows" because every row is a flow the operator launches, not a
    liveness signal.

    ONE FILE, TWO VARIANTS, and that is deliberate: the soul list and each soul's acts
    are decided HERE, once, and both presentations draw from that one decision.
      :summary  the Workflows summary card — ONE soul at a time on a 5-minute carousel
                (tasks/_agents_summary_card), the third card of the summary row
      :detail   the Workflows SIDEBAR — ONE soul at a time, every command beside what
                it launches, with Previous / Next to cycle the souls (wrapping)
    Two files each deciding chip membership is how a chip lands on one surface and not
    the other; test/lib/workflows_card_carve_out_test.rb reads the decision below.

    Locals:
      variant     :detail (default) or :summary
      card_class  extra card classes (optional) %>
<% variant = local_assigns.fetch(:variant, :detail) %>
<% card_class = ["rounded-xl border border-subtle bg-surface p-4", local_assigns[:card_class]].compact.join(" ") %>
<% launchers = heartbeat_launchers %>
<% souls = Agent.where(slug: launchers.map { |l| l[:agent_slug] }.uniq).index_by(&:slug) %>
<%# Card-specific visual order, plus the two acts deliberately NOT here.
    archive-shipped — production-deploy runs it as its final step, so the
    cleaning rides the release rather than waiting to be remembered.
    sleeper-auction-watch — the decision is settled in
    agents/turf_monster/HEARTBEAT.md (calendar-bound, operator-attended, so
    nothing should schedule it). That is the whole reason now. Its width used to
    be a second one (21 characters clipped in a two-to-a-line chip), but on the
    type scale the acts sit one to a line at xl (task hub-adopts-type-scale) and
    the slug measures 133px of a 133px text area: it fits, with no margin, so
    width neither keeps it off nor makes room for it.
    It is NOT that a chip implies a cadence — clean-infra, deploy-with-task and
    contest-rehearsal are all here, and all three are direct-invoke or
    off-sequence. That argument was retired 2026-09-09; do not restate it.
    Both acts stay invocable by name. Adding either also owes
    ACTION_DESCRIPTIONS + ACTION_ICONS keys and the arrays pinned in
    application_helper_test.rb, and test/lib/workflows_card_carve_out_test.rb
    holds THIS comment to the helper's "deliberately ABSENT" list, so a third
    carve-out cannot land here in silence. %>
<% entries = launchers.map do |launcher|
     card_actions = case launcher[:agent_slug]
                    when "carl" then ["pr-review", "pr-review-slow"]
                    when "avi" then ["qa-release", "deploy-with-task", "intent-scout"]
                    when "steffon" then ["production-deploy", "clean-infra", "workspace-launch"]
                    else launcher[:actions]
                    end
     { launcher: launcher, soul: souls[launcher[:agent_slug]], actions: card_actions }
   end %>
<% if variant == :summary %>
  <%# THE CAROUSEL STARTS ON TURF MONSTER — the operator's spec — and walks the rest in
      their canonical order, wrapping, so it reads as a circle rather than a list. %>
  <% first = entries.index { |entry| entry[:launcher][:agent_slug] == "turf-monster" } || 0 %>
  <%= render "tasks/agents_summary_card", entries: entries.rotate(first) %>
<% else %>
  <%= render "components/copy_text_script" %>
  <%# ONE SOUL AT A TIME, with Previous / Next (Alex McRitchie, 2026-11-07: "add a next
      button to the Workflows modal so the user can still cycle through the agents to
      make things quick"). A stacked list of eight souls runs past the fold, so a Next
      that only scrolled would land the next soul anywhere on screen; one soul filling
      the panel puts its every phrase in the same place on each press. The buttons
      wrap, so the panel reads as the card's wheel turned by hand, and the dots jump.
      Every soul stays in the DOM (x-show only), so the server render, the tests and
      a no-JS read still carry every launcher.

      It OPENS ON THE CARD'S SOUL: a click anywhere on the Workflows card announces the
      soul in frame (workflows-focus, from soulCarousel), so the panel shows the soul
      the operator was looking at, not Turf Monster again. %>
  <div id="heartbeats-card"
       class="<%= card_class %>"
       x-data="workflowsCycle()"
       @workflows-focus.window="show($event.detail)"
       :data-active-agent="agents[index]"
       data-active-agent="<%= entries.first&.dig(:launcher, :agent_slug) %>"
       data-agents="<%= entries.map { |entry| entry[:launcher][:agent_slug] }.join(",") %>"
       data-test="heartbeats-card">
    <p class="text-2xs text-muted">Copy any phrase to launch that soul's workflow.</p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-2" data-test="workflows-cycle-nav">
      <button type="button" @click="prev()"
              class="flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-subtle text-secondary transition hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-heading focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
              aria-label="Previous agent"
              data-test="workflows-prev"><span class="text-base leading-none" aria-hidden="true">&lsaquo;</span></button>
      <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-2xs text-muted" aria-live="polite" data-test="workflows-position">
          <span x-text="index + 1">1</span> of <%= entries.size %>
        </span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a soul" data-test="workflows-dots">
          <% entries.each_with_index do |entry, i| %>
            <% slug = entry[:launcher][:agent_slug] %>
            <%# The card's dot, the same control at the same size, so the two read as one wheel. %>
            <button type="button"
                    class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-border-strong)] transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-[var(--color-text-muted)] data-[active=true]:w-3 data-[active=true]:bg-primary"
                    data-active="<%= i.zero? %>"
                    :data-active="index === <%= i %> ? 'true' : 'false'"
                    role="tab"
                    :aria-selected="index === <%= i %> ? 'true' : 'false'"
                    aria-selected="<%= i.zero? %>"
                    aria-label="Show <%= entry[:soul]&.name.presence || slug.titleize %>"
                    data-test="workflows-dot"
                    data-agent="<%= slug %>"
                    @click="go(<%= i %>)"></button>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" @click="next()"
              class="flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-subtle text-secondary transition hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-heading focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
              aria-label="Next agent"
              data-test="workflows-next"><span class="text-base leading-none" aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4" data-test="heartbeats-list">
      <% entries.each_with_index do |entry, i| %>
        <div x-show="index === <%= i %>"
             <% unless i.zero? %>style="display: none"<% end %>
             data-test="workflows-soul"
             data-agent="<%= entry[:launcher][:agent_slug] %>">
          <%= render "tasks/heartbeat_launcher", launcher: entry[:launcher], soul: entry[:soul],
                     actions: entry[:actions], layout: :row %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
